\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Definition}
\title{The coupled coefficient functional}
\date{2026-11-09}

\p{For \vocabk{massive graded Wilson data}{fdip-00IN}, let #{Z} and #{\nu} be the positive normalizer and connection law of \ref{fdip-00IP}. For an #{\mathcal A(\mathcal V)}-valued function #{F} with bounded Borel coefficients, define the \newvocab{coupled coefficient functional}
##{\langle F\rangle=Z^{-1}\int w_g(U)\int\extd\bar\psi\,\extd\psi\;\left(F(U)\ue^{-\bar\psi(K_U\psi)}\right)\extd\lambda(U).}
At fixed #{U} put
##{\langle F\rangle_U=(\det K_U)^{-1}\int\extd\bar\psi\,\extd\psi\;\left(F(U)\ue^{-\bar\psi(K_U\psi)}\right).}
Integrals of algebra-valued functions mean integrals of their finitely many coefficients. The normalized generating polynomial is
##{\mathcal Z(\bar\eta,\eta)=Z^{-1}\int w_g(U)\mathscr Z_{K_U}(\bar\eta,\eta)\,\extd\lambda(U).}
The field and source algebras, their order and their contractions are the \vocabk{intrinsic paired construction}{fdip-00IS}.}
